Server racks, rack-mount servers, overhead cable trays and server-room pieces for Space Engineers 2: 73 blocks. Six of the servers are working automation blocks.

[i]An unofficial fan-made mod by Rioku Labs. Not made by, affiliated with or endorsed by Keen Software House.[/i]

[img]https://rioku.dev/workshop/data-center/server-room.jpg[/img]

[h2]What's in it[/h2]
Everything is in the build menu under Automation > Data Center. Sizes are width x height x depth; one grid cell is 0.25 m.

[b]Server racks (6).[/b] Server Rack (Open Frame), (Split Front Doors) and (Front + Rear Doors); the build menu's size selector picks 42U or 24U. 42U: 1.0 x 2.5 x 1.25 m, 8 slots, with an overhead cable tray and fans. 24U: 1.0 x 1.25 x 1.25 m, 4 slots. Split Front Doors have perforated leaves that swing 85° toward the aisle.

[img]https://rioku.dev/workshop/data-center/rack-servers.jpg[/img]

[b]Rack servers (10).[/b] 6U servers are 0.5 x 0.25 x 0.75 m and take one slot.
[list]
[*]Timer Server, Event Controller Server: the vanilla blocks.
[*]KVM Console: a control panel. Switch it On, or Use the drawer, and the keyboard drawer and screen come out.
[*]Status Display Server: an LCD.
[*]UPS (12U, two slots): a battery with two Power Cell bays, one on the front and one on the back.
[*]Programmable Server: an On/Off blade with a programmable block (running a program needs scripts, see below).
[*]Compute, Storage, Network Switch, Blanking Panel: decorative.
[/list]

[img]https://rioku.dev/workshop/data-center/rack-42u-front.jpg[/img]

[b]Cable trays (38).[/b] Wire-basket trays in four cable densities: Empty, Low, Moderate and Full. Straight 0.5 m and 1.5 m, Horizontal Turn, Turn Up, Turn Down, Tee and Cross in every density (28); a Drop into a rack and a Reducer in Low, Moderate and Full (6); a Long Drop Chute for half racks; Hanger Rods of 0.25, 1.0 and 2.0 m. The basket is silver; the data cables take the block's paint.

[b]Room pieces (19).[/b]
[list]
[*]Raised floor, Solid or Perforated, 0.5 or 1.0 m tiles, 0.25 m high (4).
[*]In-Row Cooler (CRAC) and PDU Cabinet, on the same footprint as a rack (2).
[*]Rack PDU (Feed A) and (Feed B) strips, for 42U and 24U racks (4).
[*]Aisle containment: sliding doors and roof panels for 1.0, 1.5 and 2.0 m aisles (6).
[*]Aisle Sign, Hanging Aisle Sign and Rack Label, all editable LCDs (3).
[/list]

[img]https://rioku.dev/workshop/data-center/kvm-open.jpg[/img]

[h2]How it works in game[/h2]
[list]
[*]Servers are their own blocks. Place a rack, then aim at the back of an empty slot to seat a server in it.
[*]The working servers behave like the vanilla block they copy and show up in the terminal as usual.
[*]Racks, the CRAC and the PDU cabinet share one footprint, so a row stays on a 1.0 m pitch. Face two rows' fronts across a cold aisle or their backs across a hot one.
[*]Lay the raised floor first; racks, cooler, cabinet and doors stand on the tiles.
[*]Containment doors go just past the row ends and block you while closed. Roof panels fit on rows of 42U racks, the CRAC and the PDU cabinet.
[*]The CRAC draws power; its fans spin and its RUN lamp lights only while it is On and powered. It does not cool anything (the game has no heat). The PDU cabinet and strips are decorative.
[*]Trays join floor to floor and work in either direction. A Reducer steps the density down one level; a Drop hangs over a rack and runs cables into it.
[*]Signs and rack labels are LCDs: type your own text, and paint the frame blue (cold) or red (hot).
[*]Blocks build like vanilla ones: a construction cage until 30 %, the frame first, lamps, screens and cables last. All have damaged models and sparks, smoke and fire; all but the Hanger Rods and the Chute break into zones. A broken section shows a solid inside with torn wiring and the big parts you would expect there, never an empty box.
[*]Until a block is complete and undamaged, its moving parts (rack sides and fan trays, KVM drawer, CRAC fans) show as still copies.
[*]Costs use vanilla components and scale with size like vanilla blocks.
[/list]

[h2]Scripts (optional)[/h2]
The mod works fully without scripts. The blocks, their build and damage states, the doors, the fans, the KVM drawer and every vanilla behavior are in the block data.

It also ships C# scripts. Space Engineers 2 runs mod scripts only when the game is started with -loadScripts; without it the game skips them and nothing breaks. With -loadScripts you also get:
[list]
[*]KVM motion: the drawer slides out, pauses, then the screen folds up and settles. Closing folds the screen first, then slides the drawer home. Without scripts both move together at a constant speed. The top slot of a 42U rack keeps the plain motion on purpose (it clears the containment rail).
[*]KVM and rack doors: behind closed doors on its front, the KVM stays stowed, comes out about 0.15 s after the doors open, and stows quickly when they start to close. Without scripts it comes out through closed doors.
[*]KVM after loading a world: it shows the right state at once. Without scripts it can show the wrong state after a load.
[*]Programmable server: Check, Run and Debug work like a programmable block, and its SCRIPT STATUS lamp and LCD bar turn green while it is On and working. Without scripts your script text is kept, Run ends in a compile error and the lamp stays amber.
[/list]
Saves are the same in both modes, so a world can go back and forth.

To turn scripts on: Steam > Library > right-click Space Engineers 2 > Properties > Launch Options, add -loadScripts. Remove it to turn them off. In multiplayer, give the server and every player the same setting.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]No other mods needed.
[*]After a game update the scripts may fail to compile until the mod is updated. The blocks then work as they do without scripts.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Front + Rear Doors racks open the front and rear doors together.
[*]Rack door leaves have no collision; a closed rack door does not stop you. Containment doors do.
[*]Two contained 1.5 m aisles cannot share a row: the second aisle's door will not place. Make one of them 1.0 m.
[*]On a 24U rack the Rack Label fits only on the back. In a contained aisle the roof covers the rack-top edge on that side, so label the open-aisle edge and sign the doors.
[*]Rack PDU strips also stand on any upward face. To seat one in a rack, aim at the plinth top in the rear corner.
[*]Hanger Rods and the Chute do not break into pieces; they only show a damaged model.
[/list]
Report bugs on GitHub with your game version and the log lines that mention [DataCenter].

